  "report": "This patient has a high estimated probability of achieving pCR (approximately 0.65). The primary driver is the HER2-positive, HR-negative tumor biology, which is highly sensitive to neoadjuvant therapy, particularly when combined with HER2-targeted agents. However, the large tumor volume (59274 mm³) and the extensive, heterogeneous enhancement pattern visible on MRI are adverse factors that lower this probability from the typical expectation for smaller HER2+ cancers. While a pCR is likely, the significant disease burden warrants close monitoring."
}
